stdout ---
Make your json look really good

Usage: jjp format [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          Output style. --mode uglify cannot be combined with --parser jsonlines or --preferred-width

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Pretty print with indentation and line breaks
          - uglify: Remove all insignificant whitespace, also known as minifying
          
          [default: pretty]

  -u, --uglify
          Shorthand for --mode uglify. --mode uglify cannot be combined with --parser jsonlines or --preferred-width

      --preferred-width <PREFERRED_WIDTH>
          Preferred maximum line width. Note this is not a hard maximum width. --preferred-width cannot be combined with --parser jsonlines or --mode uglify
          
          [default: 80]

      --end-of-line <END_OF_LINE>
          Line ending to use when formatting output

          Possible values:
          - lf:   Unix line endings (LF)
          - crlf: Windows line endings (CRLF)
          
          [default: lf]
          [alias: --eol]

      --parser <PARSER>
          Parser to use for input. --parser jsonlines cannot be combined with --mode uglify or --preferred-width

          Possible values:
          - json:      A single json document
          - jsonlines: One json document per line
          
          [default: json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
	$ echo -en "{ \"rust\":\"is a must\"   } " | jjp format
	{ "rust": "is a must" }

	$ echo -en "{ \"shoppingList\": [\"cheese\", \"slushy machine\"]   } " | jjp format --uglify
	{"shoppingList":["cheese","slushy machine"]}

